  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peacebuilding Project (PB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon has long been recognized for its rich cultural and religious diversity, as well as its post-war power-sharing arrangements. However, decades of violent and destabilizing events have continuously exposed the fragility and deep-seated fault lines of these arrangements, further straining already complex inter-communal relationships. The Lebanese system has not only weakened the relationship between citizens and the state but has also exacerbated existing inequalities, by the most vulnerable</narrative>
  </description>
